Source: homelab-database
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-database
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, postgresql, postgresql-client
Description: PostgreSQL provisioning substrate for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Installs/configures PostgreSQL itself and idempotently creates the one
 shared `homelab` database every feature's own narrow schema lives
 inside. The split-role bootstrap tool for provisioning an individual
 feature's own roles/schema (homelab-bootstrap-app-role) lives in
 homelab-common instead of here, so any feature host can depend on the
 lightweight client tool without this whole package (and a full local
 Postgres server) coming along with it.
